<title>USA: Sears Martinez to head trade group.</title>
<headline>Sears Martinez to head trade group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Retail Federation, the world's largest retail trade association, Wednesday elected Arthur Martinez, chairman and chief executive officer of Sears, Roebuck and Co, as chairman of the NRF board of directors.</p>
<p>Martinez succeeds John Shea, vice chairman, president and chief executive officer of Spiegel Inc. Last month, Shea had said he would retire from the Illinois-based catalog retailer on July 3, 1997.</p>
<p>The National Retail Federation membership includes department, specialty, discount, mass merchandise and independent stores, as well as 32 national and 50 state associations.</p>
</text>
